# Agent workspaces and local agent config. Never tracked: they carry client
# names, internal strategy, and personal detail, and this repository is
# public. Some entries are symlinks into a sibling repo (system-design,
# harden) and are local-only by design.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS. `.agents` stays above anything that would try to
# re-include a path inside it. Git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a `!` negation under an already-ignored parent can never
# re-include a file. Such a rule is silently inert: it reads as deliberate
# intent while providing none. If a path here should ever be published, the
# way to do it is to move that path out from under an ignored parent, not
# to add a negation beneath one.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately. `.claude/` matches a directory only. If
# the path is later replaced by a symlink pointing outside the repo, which
# is how these notes are kept out of a public tree, git sees a file rather
# than a directory and a trailing-slash rule stops matching it. The entry
# then silently falls out of the ignore set and `git add -A` will stage it.
# Slashless entries match a directory, a file, or a symlink.
.agents
.claude
CLAUDE.md
.vercel
